<article class="env-lemma" id="00P3">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/00P3">Lemma <span data-tag="00P3">10.116.5</span>.</a> Let $k$ be a field. Let $S$ be a finite type $k$-algebra. Let $K/k$ be a field extension. Then $\dim (S) = \dim (K \otimes _ k S)$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      By Lemma <a href="/tag/00OY" data-tag="00OY">10.115.4</a> there exists a finite injective map $k[y_1, \ldots , y_ d] \to S$ with $d = \dim (S)$. Since $K$ is flat over $k$ we also get a finite injective map $K[y_1, \ldots , y_ d] \to K \otimes _ k S$. The result follows from Lemma <a href="/tag/00OK" data-tag="00OK">10.112.4</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>